	(text "Design intent (revision 2, decision 12; nothing here is simulated or measured)\nPROPOSED   Chain: S12023-10 APD, OPA857 TIA (20k/5k), AC coupling C51/R51, OPA855 non-inverting gain 7, 68 MHz\n           low-pass, AC coupling C55/R59 to SDET_P. DC level of the whole post-amp path is VCM_REF (1.65 V\n           from the Monitor sheet), so the output idles at the comparator baseline.\nPROPOSED   Stage 2 HV filter R50 10k (1206, 200 V) + C50 10n (1210, 500 V C0G) at the cathode; stage 1 is on\n           the Power sheet. HV_K is up to 220 V: keep-out to TIA_IN (200 V creepage/clearance), no HV test\n           points.\nVERIFIED   OPA857 (SBOS630D): bias APD cathode to positive supply, anode to IN, so the output swings DOWN\n           below OUTN = 1.83 V (p.19, 8.2.1.2 step 2; p.15, 7.3.1). Test_SD (13) GND, Test_IN (14) 3V3 (p.4\n           pin table). CTRL 1 = 20k, 0 = 5k (p.6).\nVERIFIED   OPA855 (SBOS622D): FB (pin 1) is internally the amplifier output; RF goes FB to IN- on the same\n           side of the package, OUT drives the load, NC pin 2 stays open (p.17, 8.3.2, Fig. 8-4). PD high =\n           on, enable threshold 1.5 V typ / 1.8 V max above VS-; PD bias 70 uA typ, 140 uA max (p.7), so PD\n           goes straight to 3V3 (a 10k would drop 0.7-1.4 V). Thermal pad to VS- (p.20, 8.4.1; p.29).\nVERIFIED   OPA855 input common-mode 1.3 V max low to 2.7 V min high at VS+ = 3.3 V (p.6): VCM_REF 1.65 V is\n           inside. Overdrive recovery 3 ns (p.6). Datasheet gain-7 test values are RF 453 / RG about 75 (Fig.\n           7-3, p.15); no RF/RG table exists, so 301/49.9 (G = 7.03) is PROPOSED: lower resistances load the\n           output less than the test values on a 3.3 V part. UNRESOLVED: stability with RF 301 not checked.\nPROPOSED   RG returns to PA_REF = VCM_REF through R60 10 ohm with C53 1u to GND, so gain is referenced to the\n           baseline and the 1u cap does not load the Monitor sheet's VCM_REF buffer. Input return R51 1k to\n           VCM_REF (corner 1.6 kHz, 100 us). OPA855 IB -12 uA typ (p.6) into 1k gives about +80 mV output\n           offset (derived), which moves the idle point to about 1.73 V, close to the 1.75 V mid-swing of the\n           1.15 to 2.35 V output limits (p.7).\nPROPOSED   Clip level (derived): 1.15 Vpp / (7 x 18.2k) = 9 uA at 20k, 36.5 uA at 5k; OPA857 saturates at 60\n           uA / 240 uA (p.15, 7.3.1). Output is AC coupled after the clipping amplifier so clipping is\n           symmetric about the baseline.\nPROPOSED   Low-pass R56 49.9 + C54 47p = 68 MHz (research 60-80 MHz). SDET_P: C55 100n, R59 1k to VCM_REF\n           (matched to the 1k on the Slicer's IN- side). TP10 PA_OUT, TP11 SDET_P, TP12 TIA_REF. TIA_TAP =\n           TIA_OUT through R58 1k to the RSSI detector.\nUNRESOLVED OPA857 stability and bandwidth at 6 pF source capacitance (datasheet characterises 1.5 pF, p.6).\n           OPA855 stability at G = 7 into the 49.9 ohm / 47 pF load not simulated. Received power not\n           measured."
		(exclude_from_sim yes)
